.env
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.DS_Store
.coverage
htmlcov/
# The database is a BUILD ARTEFACT, not a source file. `sqeual db build` is
# deterministic — a fixed seed and a fixed sequence of draws — so the generator
# plus `data/schema.sql` reproduce it exactly, and both of those are committed.
# A 700 KB binary in Git would be a thing nobody can review, that changes
# wholesale on every regeneration, and that a reader has to trust matches the
# DDL beside it. `sqeual db build` prints a row digest so two builds can be
# compared without diffing binaries.
#
# Anchored to the repository root, so a future `src/sqeual/data/` cannot be
# caught by it.
/data/*.db
/data/*.db-journal
/data/*.db-wal

# Every run holds a question somebody asked and the rows that came back. That is
# exactly the material a repository should not carry, and it is a build artefact
# besides: `sqeual ask` writes it and nothing reads it back.
#
# `runs/eval/<ts>/` is the same rule for the same reason at forty times the size:
# an evaluation holds every golden question, both result digests, and the SQL a
# model wrote for each. What is committed instead is the evidence a reader needs
# — `docs/examples/*.live.md` and `*.synthetic.md`, chosen by a person and
# labelled banner-first — rather than every run anybody happened to make.
/runs/
